  "i": [
   {
    "id": "i1",
    "kind": "Javadoc",
    "lines": [
     7,
     14
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests that {@link TokenQueue#consumeElementSelector()} correctly unescapes backslash-escaped CSS special characters when reading element selectors. <p>In CSS selector syntax a backslash followed by a special character (e.g. {@code \\.}) means \"treat the special character literally\". The selector consumer must strip the escape prefix and return the bare character in the result.</p>"
   },
   {
    "id": "i2",
    "kind": "Javadoc",
    "lines": [
     17,
     35
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Verifies that a queue containing four space-separated element selectors, each with a different backslash-escaped special character, is consumed correctly. <p>Input queue (Java string literal): {@code \"p\\\\\\\\p p\\\\.p p\\\\:p p\\\\!p\"} <br>Actual characters in the queue: {@code p\\\\p p\\.p p\\:p p\\!p} <p>Each selector uses a CSS escape sequence: <ul> <li>{@code p\\\\p} — escaped backslash → {@code p\\p}</li> <li>{@code p\\.p} — escaped dot → {@code p.p}</li> <li>{@code p\\:p} — escaped colon → {@code p:p}</li> <li>{@code p\\!p} — escaped exclamation → {@code p!p}</li> </ul> <p>Between selectors, whitespace must be consumed (and the method must return {@code true} to indicate that at least one whitespace character was seen). After the last selector the queue must be empty."
   },
   {
    "id": "i3",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     38,
     38
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Queue content (actual chars): p\\\\p p\\.p p\\:p p\\!p"
   },
   {
    "id": "i4",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     41,
     41
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "\"p\\\\p\" → backslash is itself escaped, so the result is a literal backslash"
   },
   {
    "id": "i5",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     44,
     44
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Separator between selectors must be present and consumed"
   },
   {
    "id": "i6",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     47,
     47
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "\"p\\.p\" → dot is a CSS special char; the escape strips the backslash, leaving \".\""
   },
   {
    "id": "i7",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     52,
